  "notes": [
    "Phone numbers are read one digit at a time: 三九七四 is sān jiǔ qī sì, often grouped in pairs: sānjiǔ qīsì. In phone numbers 一 is usually said yāo, so it does not sound like 七 (qī).",
    "你多大了？ is for a child or someone your age. To an older person, say 您多大年纪了？ (Nín duō dà niánjì le?).",
    "岁 (suì) comes after the age: 我三十岁 (wǒ sānshí suì)."
